<title>NORWAY: N.Sea oil loadings suspended, output normal.</title>
<headline>N.Sea oil loadings suspended, output normal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>High winds prevented offshore oil loadings at the North Sea Statfjord and Gullfaks fields on Friday, but all production was normal, operator Den norske oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said.</p>
<p>Two shuttle tankers were waiting to load at the Gullfaks development and one at Statfjord, a Statoil spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We had to stop loading last night but all production is normal. The wind is beginning to drop now and we hope to begin (loading) again later tonight,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Offshore crude loadings are often disrupted by high winds and swell in the winter months. The maximum permitted wave height for tankers to moor up to the loading buoys is 4.5 metres.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
